Package: CanPAS
Type: Package
Title: Cancer Prognosis Analysis Suite
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: person("Jin", "Wang", email = "Jinwang93@suda.edu.cn",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A survival-analysis toolkit for public cancer cohorts. It serves
    expression matrices and survival tables from a curated GEO/CGGA mirror over
    a public REST API and from TCGA through UCSC Xena with local clinical
    tables, and exposes one uniform "merged data" schema. Endpoints are requested
    by family (OS, DSS, DFS, PFS, MFS), and the token a cohort actually reports is
    resolved per cohort and returned with every result, so cohorts are never
    pooled across families. Functions cover gene and signature scoring,
    Kaplan-Meier and cut-point analysis, univariable and multivariable Cox
    models, time-dependent ROC, cross-cohort random-effects meta-analysis, pooled
    Kaplan-Meier with a prediction interval, and competing risks, with five
    statistical safeguards disclosed by default. A bundled Shiny application
    drives the same exported functions.
